00:07:46.960 --> 00:07:52.440
From black hole feedback to the chemistry of solar system formation. Astronomers have compiled

00:07:52.440 --> 00:07:59.220
deuterium to hydrogen ratios from multiple comets observed over recent decades. The values differ

00:07:59.220 --> 00:08:06.260
between Jupiter family and or cloud comets, pointing to distinct formation regions. These isotopic

00:08:06.260 --> 00:08:12.580
fingerprints survive in the icies that make up comet nuclei. Comparing the ratios with those measured

00:08:12.580 --> 00:08:18.120
in Earth's oceans helps test whether comets delivered a significant fraction of terrestrial water.

00:08:18.980 --> 00:08:24.880
New measurements from upcoming comet encounters will expand the sample. The work ties directly into

00:08:24.880 --> 00:08:31.380
models of how the proto-planetary disk mixed material. From solar system chemistry to an easy

00:08:31.380 --> 00:08:39.840
naked eye target this week. The coma star cluster, also known as Mellot 111, spans about 4 degrees in

00:08:39.840 --> 00:08:46.340
the constellation Coma Baraneseese. At roughly 40 degrees above the western horizon after sunset.

